  "reading": "The raw SPSC tick ring is the channel; the full pipeline is the product. The ring can exceed 1M ticks/s in pure Python. The full pipeline cannot in pure Python: each entry costs ~2 canonical-JSON serialisations + 2 HMAC-SHA256 + 3 SHA-256 (~30us/entry in-process). Reaching millions of entries/sec for the full pipeline needs a compiled hot path (a C/Rust extension, or a reimplementation of the per-entry hashing) and/or a cheaper per-entry scheme (fewer hash ops, precomputed canonical forms, batched hashing)."
